from http://www.openbsd.org/hppa.html :

Supported models

The rule of thumb is: if it weighs more than 25kg --
most likely it is not supported.


FreeBSD is a volunteer project, volunteers don't have
every hardware combination, volunteers don't get time
to support every configuration.
The models with the best support are the desktop models,
there just ain't a lot of people with ES40's in their
bikeshed.

When you choose to run Linux or BSD you've got 3 ways
to solve problems you might encounter:

- Solve them yourself
- Give somebody money/hardware to solve them
- Ask really nicely on the mailinglists,
   and somebody might do it for free.

The only "supported" option for alpha servers is Tru64,
anything else is unsupported.


FreeBSD alpha was moved to a tier2 platform for FreeBSD 5,
because hp has stopped developing the platform, and because
the project wanted to focus on amd64 and sparc64
( the lengthy and more correct explanation can
   be found on the lists ).



